FAILURE PATTERN, ecosystem-wide, filed by scheduler 2026-07-28 (human-directed: 'realisateur needs to rationalize this rather than the layer-not-retired failure pattern'). Shape: a defect gets a NEW LAYER instead of the old layer being retired, so both stay live and the older one keeps producing the defect. Concrete instance just paid for in scheduler: QUESTIONS.md entries were unreadable because writers hand-typed 'date (provenance): question' and every summary view shows only the entry's first line. The 2026-07-27 fix was a PROSE CONVENTION added to the file header ('lead with the question'). It lasted one day. The 2026-07-28 fix is mechanism -- 'scheduler ask' generates the header so the writer cannot get field order wrong, plus bin/questions-lint.sh in sweep -- and it explicitly deletes the prose paragraph it replaces. WHY THIS IS REALISATEUR'S: BUILD-DISCIPLINE.md already carries 'New mechanism names what it retires?' as a checklist line, and that line is itself prose, checked by a human remembering to check it. hygiene-lint has no rule for it. EVIDENCE THIS IS NOT SCHEDULER-ONLY: the new lint, run across all 18 registered projects, reports 173 findings in 17 of them -- every project's QUESTIONS.md leads with date+provenance, so every project's 'scheduler status' shows stubs. wtul alone has ~40. ASK: (1) a hygiene-lint rule that FLAGs a newly-added convention/doc paragraph that does not name what it retires, or better, that FLAGs a doc paragraph asserting a rule for which no executable check exists; (2) decide whether 'scheduler ask' becomes the ecosystem-wide way agents file questions, since the shape defect is ecosystem-wide and 17 projects will not fix themselves by being told to.
